  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only PCA with multiprofile avgpool is the strongest setting so far (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), clearly better than singleprofile PCA and transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet is weak. The key uncertainty is whether this multiprofile avgpool benefit is specific to PCA or also holds for learned RNA representations. config_005 tests scvi_n200 in the same multiprofile avgpool setting, changing only the RNA encoder relative to config_002. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the most promising direction, isolates the representation effect, and will guide whether to invest further in learned RNA encoders or multimodal fusion."
